  "aboutParagraphs": [
    "Veteran's Park is one of Arlington's originals — an 18-hole course from 1988 that mixes hilly, rugged holes through mesquite brush and cactus with open park fairways. From the standard pins it plays 4,073 feet at par 54, with the brush making the short holes sneakier than they look.",
    "Free to play with concrete tees and DISCatcher baskets, it's the kind of course where the terrain does the teaching. The rugged holes have genuine Texas character — expect thorns, hills, and a few laughs.",
    "A friendly, characterful round that's been a DFW staple for over three decades."
  ],
