  "signatureHoleDescription": "Hole 12 is the longest at Veteran's Park at 395 feet — a par 3 that climbs the course's best hill with the mesquite closing in on both sides. It's the hole that gives the short course its one big moment, and the one where the Texas terrain really shows up.",
  "localTips": "The brush and cactus are real — wear sturdy shoes and watch your discs. Free to play with an old-school park-course feel. The hilly holes are the memorable ones; bring a putter and enjoy the character.",
